# MyChat modularity

Preserve the current layout. Do not collapse back into a monolithic `index.html` or a single mega `app.js`.

## Layout

```
index.html          markup only — .shell > sidebar + .workspace (topbar/stage/dock)
css/main.css        @imports by region (tokens → base → sidebar → topbar/settings/chat/composer/animations)
js/app.js           composition root: DOM refs, mutable state, event listeners, wiring
js/config.js        constants, models, keys, tools, regexes — no DOM, no I/O
js/chat.js          chat turn pipeline (Ollama + tools + stream)
js/image.js         Flux generate / refine
js/ui.js            DOM helpers (bubbles, cards, banners, status)
js/session.js       multi-chat library (v3 localStorage) + active thread persist/restore
js/export.js        thread → Markdown download
js/intent.js        Chat | Image (explicit; no Auto)
js/markdown.js      think tags + safe Markdown (links open in new tab)
js/util.js          StoppedError, abort detection, escapeHtml
js/memory/*         conversation, facts, summarizer, rag, orchestrator facade
serve.py            static + /api/search + /api/rag/* (no chat proxy)
memory/rag_store.py chunk → embed → retrieve
```

## Boundaries

- **UI transcript** (`threadLog`) ≠ **model history** (`memory/conversation`). Keep both.
- **Chat library** ≠ single session: `session.js` owns `{ activeId, chats[] }`; migrate v1/v2 on load.
- Facts & RAG are global across chats; clearing/deleting a chat must not wipe them.
- Pipelines take **injected deps** / factories (`createUi`, `createChatRunner`, …). Do not reach into `app.js` globals from leaf modules.
- Browser talks to Ollama directly; `serve.py` only serves files + search + RAG.
- Put new feature code in the owning module; grow `app.js` only for state + wiring.

## Module headers

Every JS/CSS/Python module starts with a short **Intent** + **Architecture** block. **Quality: N/10** is written by the Boy Scout **scoring sub-agent** at the end of each edit batch (see `mychat-boyscout.mdc`) — not invented by the editing agent.

## ❌ Avoid

- Inline `<style>` / large `<script>` in `index.html`
- Importing `location` / DOM at top-level in modules that Node tests may load (use getters like `getSearchApi()`)
- Mixing chat streaming logic into `ui.js`, or DOM building into `chat.js`
- Deleting golden-path / memory tests when changing history, tools, or RAG
